@startuml patient-journey-sequence
title The Patient Journey — Registration through Payment (with Kafka events)

actor Patient
participant "patient-portal" as Portal
participant "api-gateway" as Gateway
participant "auth-service" as Auth
participant "patient-service" as PatientSvc
participant "doctor-service" as DoctorSvc
participant "appointment-service" as ApptSvc
participant "notification-service" as Notify
participant "ml-prediction-service" as ML
participant "encounter-service" as Encounter
participant "insurance-service" as Insurance
participant "triage-service" as Triage
participant "ehr-service" as EHR
participant "prescription-service" as Rx
participant "lab-service" as Lab
participant "pharmacy-inventory-service" as Pharmacy
participant "billing-service" as Billing
participant "payment-service" as Payment
participant "document-service" as Document
queue "Kafka" as Kafka
participant "audit-service" as Audit

note over Kafka, Audit
  audit-service consumes every event throughout the journey (not drawn per-step for clarity)
end note

== 1. Registration ==
Patient -> Portal: Fill registration form
Portal -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/patients
Gateway -> Auth: Validate / issue token
Gateway -> PatientSvc: POST /api/v1/patients
PatientSvc -> PatientSvc: Create patient (local tx + outbox)
PatientSvc -> Kafka: publish PatientRegistered
Kafka -> Notify: consume PatientRegistered
Notify -> Patient: Welcome SMS/email

== 2. Browse doctors and available slots ==
Patient -> Portal: Search doctors / specialities
Portal -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/doctors, GET /api/v1/slots
Gateway -> DoctorSvc: GET /api/v1/doctors
Gateway -> ApptSvc: GET /api/v1/slots?doctorId=...

== 3. Book an appointment ==
Patient -> Portal: Select slot
Portal -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/appointments
Gateway -> ApptSvc: POST /api/v1/appointments
ApptSvc -> ApptSvc: Optimistic-locked UPDATE slot\n(version check, 409 on conflict)
ApptSvc -> Kafka: publish AppointmentBooked
Kafka -> Notify: consume AppointmentBooked
Notify -> Patient: SMS confirmation
Kafka -> ML: consume AppointmentBooked
ML -> ML: Compute no-show risk score

== 4. Reminder, 24h before ==
Notify -> Notify: Scheduled job (Celery)
Notify -> Patient: Reminder SMS/email

== 5. Arrival and check-in ==
Patient -> Portal: Check in
Portal -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/encounters
Gateway -> Encounter: POST /api/v1/encounters
Encounter -> Encounter: Create encounter, state = CHECKED_IN
Encounter -> Insurance: GET eligibility (sync REST)
Insurance --> Encounter: Eligibility result
Encounter -> Triage: POST /api/v1/triage (if emergency)
Triage --> Encounter: ESI level 1-5

== 6. Consultation ==
Encounter -> Encounter: transition -> IN_CONSULTATION
Encounter -> EHR: POST /api/v1/ehr (clinical note, ICD-10)
Encounter -> Rx: POST /api/v1/prescriptions
Encounter -> Lab: POST /api/v1/labs (lab order placed)

== 7. Laboratory ==
Lab -> Lab: Record result, verify, release
Lab -> Kafka: publish LabResultReady
Kafka -> Notify: consume LabResultReady
Notify -> Patient: Result-ready notice
Kafka -> Encounter: consume LabResultReady (clinical lifecycle)
Kafka -> EHR: consume LabResultReady (attach to record)
Kafka -> Billing: consume LabResultReady (charge line)

== 8. Pharmacy ==
Rx -> Pharmacy: Dispense request
Pharmacy -> Pharmacy: Decrement stock on dispense\n(reservation -> dispensed)

== 9. Discharge ==
Encounter -> Encounter: transition -> READY_FOR_DISCHARGE -> COMPLETED
Encounter -> Kafka: publish EncounterCompleted

== 10. Invoicing ==
Kafka -> Billing: consume EncounterCompleted
Billing -> Billing: Assemble invoice\n(consultation + labs + drugs + bed)
Billing -> Insurance: Request split (sync REST)
Insurance --> Billing: Insurer share / patient share
Billing -> Insurance: Submit claim
Billing -> Kafka: publish InvoiceIssued
Kafka -> Notify: consume InvoiceIssued
Notify -> Patient: Invoice notice
Kafka -> Document: consume InvoiceIssued
Document -> Document: Render invoice PDF

== 11. Payment ==
Patient -> Portal: Pay invoice
Portal -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/payments (Idempotency-Key)
Gateway -> Payment: POST /api/v1/payments
Payment -> Payment: Create PaymentAttempt (PROCESSING)

alt success
  Payment -> Payment: Gateway confirms capture
  Payment -> Kafka: publish PaymentCompleted
  Kafka -> Billing: consume PaymentCompleted\n(invoice -> PAID / PARTIALLY_PAID)
  Kafka -> Document: consume PaymentCompleted
  Document -> Document: Generate PDF receipt
  Kafka -> Notify: consume PaymentCompleted
  Notify -> Patient: Payment confirmation
else failure (saga compensation)
  Payment -> Kafka: publish PaymentFailed
  Kafka -> Billing: consume PaymentFailed\n(invoice reverts to PENDING)
  Kafka -> Pharmacy: consume PaymentFailed\n(release reservation or write-off/return-to-stock)
  Kafka -> Notify: consume PaymentFailed
  Notify -> Patient: Payment-failure notice + retry link
end

note over Kafka, Audit
  Throughout every step: audit-service records every access to patient data
end note

@enduml
